This is a **local operator wiki**, not the public project documentation. It is excluded through `.git/info/exclude` and is not part of the GitHub push. It contains no credentials or private journal text.

## Latest recorded state

A fresh [management installation on Marvin](08-management-install.md) is running
as `mrmr.service` from `/home/heath/mrmr`. Open
**https://marvin.tail91529e.ts.net:8445/manage/** on the tailnet and unlock with the
privately stored operator token. It is in protected first-run setup: no model,
source, or live effect is configured, and ingestion is blocked until activation.
No inference runtime was installed on Marvin.

The UI supports drafts, shadow activation/recovery, source controls, review, and
bounded evaluation. See the current [management guide](../README.md#configuration-and-management-ui),
[setup runbook](../SETUP.md), and [delivery status](../DASHBOARD_ROADMAP.md).

The former Marvin installation was removed with approval: the mrmr service,
installation directory (including its database, credentials, and backups), and
Tailscale `/dashboard/` route are gone. Marvin's LFM2.5 service, model, and local
inference runtime were also removed. Do not use the old paths or URLs as current
access instructions. The new installation uses separate paths and port 8445;
its checks are recorded in the [installation note](08-management-install.md).

The [October 26 dashboard deployment](07-dashboard.md) and pages below are
historical records. Deepthought model/service descriptions and the offline setup
atlas are snapshots, not evidence of current service health.

## Historical state — 2026-10-15

- **Marvin:** mrmr is running as the enabled user service `mrmr-shadow.service`.
- **Deepthought:** Nemotron 3.5 Super VL and native d1-3B CUDA BF16 are running together. Both services are enabled. Qwen is stopped, disabled, and retained for rollback.
- **Journal input:** exact system units, warning or higher, checked every 30 seconds. Root and regular-UID canaries passed. User services such as Hermes remain excluded.
- **Discord:** one separate, clearly marked setup test received confirmed delivery. Real-event notifications are still **shadowed**.
- **Actions:** no service changes, automatic investigator tasks, or worker harness are enabled.
- **Existing workloads:** Plex, Hermes, LFM2.5, Tailscale, and SSH socket activation remain healthy.

## Read the wiki

Open the [interactive setup atlas](setup.html) in a browser. It is one offline file with a selectable system map, synthetic event playback, measured results, a memory-guard simulator, and service commands. It cannot connect to the running setup or perform an effect.

1. [Runtime and code changes](01-runtime.md)
